<title>ARGENTINA: Saloman Bros cuts Argentine weighting, ups Mexico.</title>
<headline>Saloman Bros cuts Argentine weighting, ups Mexico.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saloman Brothers said Monday it was cutting its model equity portfolio weight for Argentina to 8.5 percent from 9.5 percent and boosting Mexico to 23.0 percent from 22.0 percent.</p>
<p>&quot;We are shifting 1.0 percent of our model portfolio from Argentina's telecom sector into Mexico's conglomerates, steel and pulp/paper sectors. With these changes, Argentina's underweight position becomes more pronounced,&quot; Salomon Brothers said in a statement.</p>
</text>
